sbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MICHIKATA, YUUSEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TARUMI, KIYOHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUOKA, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermal spray material which comprises: at least 5 vol.% at least one double oxide containing (a) at least one trivalent metal element selected among Al, Ti, V, Cr, Fe, Co, Rh, In, and rare earth elements (Sc, Y, and lanthanoid) and (b) at least one of the rare earth elements (Sc, Y, and lanthanoid) different from those in (a); and as the remainder at least one of the oxides of metals excluding Group Ia metals and of the oxides of Si.  When the material is used to conduct thermal spraying, a coating film having excellent mechanical and chemical properties is obtained efficiently.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une substance de pulvérisation thermique qui renferme au moins 5 % en vol. d'au moins un double oxyde contenant: a) au moins un élément métallique trivalent choisi parmi Al, Ti, V, Cr, Fe, Co, Rh, In, et des éléments du groupe des terres rares (Sc, Y, et lanthanide); et b) au moins un desdits éléments du groupe des terres rares(Sc, Y, et lanthanide) différent de ceux de a). Le solde de cette substance est constitué d'au moins un des oxydes de métaux, à l'exception des métaux du groupe Ia et des oxydes de Si. Lorsque l'on utilise la substance de cette invention pour effectuer une pulvérisation thermique, on obtient efficacement un film de revêtement présentant d'excellentes propriétés mécaniques et chimiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>